[0.0-1.2] spk0: Hello?
[1.7-7.7] spk1: Good afternoon, Mrs. Kowalski! I am thrilled to tell you that your entry won our second-place prize!
[8.2-11.6] spk0: Did I? I enter those magazine puzzles all the time!
[12.1-19.3] spk1: You won twenty-five thousand dollars! Before our courier delivers the check, we just need the federal withholding fee.
[19.8-23.8] spk0: Can't you just take the taxes right out of the prize money?
[24.3-31.1] spk1: Federal sweepstakes law requires the winner to pay the eight hundred dollar insurance and tax stamp up front.
[31.6-35.2] spk0: I suppose that makes sense if it's the government rule.
[35.7-42.1] spk1: Exactly. Once you send a cashier's check to our claims agent in Delaware, we release the funds.
